<title>USA: Riddell Sports Inc Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Riddell Sports Inc Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>RIDDELL SPORTS INC.</p>
<p>				  Financial Highlights</p>
<p>		  (Dollars in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>				Third Quarter	     Nine Months</p>
<p>			     Ended Sept. 30,   Ended Sept. 30,</p>
<p>			 1996	 1995		 1996	1995</p>
<p> Net revenues   $18,337    $17,700	    $59,793   $55,023</p>
<p>Cost of goods sold</p>
<p>		     10,100     10,027	     31,316    29,345</p>
<p> Gross margin     8,237	7,673	     28,477    25,678</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>			6,447	6,030	     21,977    20,026</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>			1,790	1,643		6,500     5,652</p>
<p> Interest expense   785	  802		2,176     2,192</p>
<p>Income before tax</p>
<p>			1,005	  841		4,324     3,460</p>
<p> Income taxes (a)    40	   38		  190	 156</p>
<p> Net income (a)     965	  803		4,134     3,304</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>  per share (a)    0.11	 0.10		 0.48	0.41</p>
<p>Average common and common</p>
<p>equivalent shares</p>
<p>outstanding (000's)</p>
<p>  Primary	   8,568	8,068		8,548     8,068</p>
<p>  Fully diluted   8,634	8,068		8,616     8,068</p>
<p>    (a)   For all periods shown above, income tax expense was</p>
<p>reduced by the benefit of a net operating loss carryforward recognized during the periods.  The recognition of these tax benefits had the effect of decreasing tax expense, and increasing net income, for the three month periods ended Sept.</p>
<p>30, 1996 and 1995 by approximately $340, or $0.04 per share, and $280, or $0.03 per share, respectively, and for the nine month periods ended Sept. 30, 1996 and 1995 by approximately $1,470, or $0.17 per share, and $1,150, or $0.14 per share, respectively.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
